
== yeast / u_t = r*u*(1 - u/K) / random
equation: u_t = r*u*(1 - u/K)
          target u(t); fit K, r
split: random, 15 points to train, 4 held out

rank model                              held-out error    time   fitted
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
1  = Neural network (data only)                  2.391    4.1s   -
2  = Polynomial + equation                       2.947    4.5s   K=663.2, r=0.5464
3  = Equation fit (classical)                    2.961    2.9s   K=663.1, r=0.5465
4  = PINN (neural network + equation)            2.962    5.7s   K=662.9, r=0.5469
5    Smoothing spline (data only)                3.714    0.8s   -
6    Polynomial (data only)                      4.559    0.0s   -

best: Equation fit (classical). Held-out error is the RMS error on data the models never saw.
=     4 models are within the noise of the lowest error on these 4 held-out points, so the data cannot tell them apart.
      The one with the fewest free numbers is returned; pick="lowest" would return Neural network (data only).

